sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XV: eggs as solids of revolution of a definite, species-varying family of ovoid meridian curves (Preston 1953 family on Biggins et al. 2018 / Deeming 2018 data) — MorphoEval overall 56.1/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py` (overall weighted score: 56.1/100). The v1 script implements the Preston (1953) ovoid meridian family with Biggins et al. (2018) shape indices, a closed-form polar-asymmetry index (r = 0.99997 against the published numeric index on 1389 eggs) and an exact volume functional, reproduces the published guillemot C126 coefficients, shows the 30-species elongation table, the 1389-egg morphospace and Thompson's relative-egg-size prediction (Deeming PC2 vs egg/female mass, Spearman rho = 0.391, p = 6.7e-8), and animates sphere -> guillemot within the family. It does not exercise Thompson's envelope equation in code, performs no parameter sweep, never segments the five vendored specimen photographs (so the solid-of-revolution part of the claim is untested), has no negative / ablation control (Steiner Cartesian oval, Baker / Troscianko / Carter alternatives), no eta^2 / KS statistics, no runtime SHA-256 verification, and no CLI parameter overrides. Overall 56.1/100 (faithfulness 52.3, reproducibility 64.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 83b41df2a; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 62, Morphological realism / specimen match 42, Parameter expressivity 50, Morphometric validation 58, Source and data traceability 70, Code-to-model traceability 66, Reproducibility package 60. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_034_on_the_shapes_of_eggs_and_of_c_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py at 83b41df2a, image/png, 301794 B, 1540×1100 px, artifact_sha256 6b6ab119d0c53b000d31126af07540589cb3cefe66a034128faca3bb8eb7e566 (sha256 6b6ab119d0c53b000d31126af07540589cb3cefe66a034128faca3bb8eb7e566), spec_fingerprint 7f3cb7ceffd0305bc161370b241783acb708b5e9be3e83c757bf5c363fc7a7f4. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7f3cb7ceffd0305bc161370b241783acb708b5e9be3e83c757bf5c363fc7a7f4; artifact_sha256: 6b6ab119d0c53b000d31126af07540589cb3cefe66a034128faca3bb8eb7e566; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/biggins2018_C126_uria_aalge_silhouette.jpg=0a5c73b782104608..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/biggins2018_comparison_of_fits.csv=b2712450e2f2132e..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/biggins2018_data_for_comparing_indices.csv=39a776b94bad894a..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/biggins2018_range_of_egg_shapes.csv=3d0617dfd8cd0c20..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/deeming2018_jab_egg_shape_composition.csv=6367ba5252e52fcd..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/mwnh_0308_vanellus_vanellus_eggs.jpg=426b26bbad6c67d2..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/mwnh_0481_uria_aalge_eggs.jpg=fcaadba0ae209c4c..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/mwnh_0646_strix_aluco_egg.jpg=139f2249abb44e77..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/mwnh_1921_podiceps_cristatus_eggs.jpg=866eb96ea90025cc..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/paper_citations.bib=45e263a3bef66328..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/scout_manifest.json=83406c03aa7136ec..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/t1917_034_on_the_shapes_of_eggs_and_of_c_reference.json=65a558575446b312...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson 1917 p. 652: eggs are simple solids of revolution; forms range from spherical (owl, penguin, tortoise) through ellipsoidal (grebe, cormorant, pelican) and ovoid (hen) to blunt-pointed conical (guillemot, puffin, sandpiper, plover, curlew); prolate never oblate. | Thompson 1917 p. 655 (5): the most unsymmetrical / tapered eggs are large relative to the parent bird. | Thompson 1917 p. 658: envelope equation p_n + T(1/r + 1/r') = P.; reconstructed_in_script: Preston (1953) four-parameter meridian family y = (c0 + c1 x + c2 x^2 + c3 x^3) sqrt(1 - x^2) with Biggins et al. (2018) indices and a closed-form polar asymmetry R_pole = p(+/-1)^2. | Closed-form volume of the solid of revolution 315 V / (4 pi (L/2)^3) = 105 c0^2 + 21 (c1^2 + 2 c0 c2) + 9 (c2^2 + 2 c1 c3) + 5 c3^2. | Species-mean elongation table (30 species), 1389-egg morphospace, Deeming PC2 vs relative egg mass Spearman test.; transfer_boundary: The Preston family is a 1953 descriptor adopted as the quantitative reading of Thompson's 'definite family'; Thompson himself gave no algebraic family (he rejected Steiner's Cartesian oval). | Biggins et al. (2018) eggs are auks and penguins (plus a 10-egg range set); order-level breadth comes only from Deeming's PCs.; does_not_claim: That the oviduct pressure mechanism (Thompson pp. 654-660) is the cause of the family; only the geometric claim is tested. | Anything about eggshell microstructure, colour, or non-avian hard-shelled eggs beyond Thompson's mention.." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add negative / ablation controls: Steiner's Cartesian oval r + m r' = c on the guillemot outline (Thompson p. 654 footnote), prolate ellipsoid (c1 = c2 = c3 = 0) and Baker / Troscianko / Carter error ratios from biggins2018_comparison_of_fits.csv.",
            "remediation needed: Add runtime SHA-256 verification of the 13 pinned dataset files, CLI overrides (--pole-contrast, --equator-contrast, --frames, --skip-gif, --verify-only), expand self_test() with integrity and two-run determinism checks, document page / theorem cross-references per function, and write datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/result.json.",
            "remediation needed: Add statistics: Preston RMSE / breadth distribution, between-species eta^2 and Kruskal-Wallis for Elongation / Pointedness / PolarAsymmetry (30 species) and order-level eta^2 for Deeming PC1 / PC2, KS test of species elongation distributions (guillemot vs penguin), Pearson r of segmented vs published C126 profile.",
            "remediation needed: Exercise Thompson's envelope equation in code: implement the pole / equator curvature closure of the Preston family (given pole pressure contrast, equatorial pressure and volume solve for c0..c3), sweep the pole pressure contrast to generate sphere -> ovoid -> conical eggs, and compute the implied (P - p_n)/T mean-curvature profile for every Biggins egg (uniform pressure <=> sphere; pole tension sign).",
            "remediation needed: Segment the five vendored specimen photographs (Otsu / multi-Otsu threshold, convex hull, watershed), extract upper and lower meridian profiles, test axisymmetry (RMS upper-vs-lower / half-breadth), fit the Preston family by Biggins' weighted least squares and compare C126 against the published coefficients; place owl, grebe, lapwing and guillemot in the morphospace." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.561"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 228 Pass 1 Assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

